    "_note": "Each floor's temperature (#393, sim/temperature.ts), all in °C (the UI shows °F by default). Floor 1's resting temperature is rolled per hole from a band set by its latitude: restBands' bands, straight-line by latitude between them and on past the first toward the equator, never above restCapC (50 °F). The starter's band (20-25°) is 40-45 °F, the poles' 0-15 °F. Deeper floors rest a little warmer. Heat is measured against a reference floor, a small hole's floor dug out across its unlocked rings: a heater's `heats` is how far it lifts that floor at full power; smaller floors lift more, bigger ones less (never counting fewer than minCells cells). Heaters warm a floor at their lift a game day each (more heaters, faster); with no heat, a floor drifts toward rest at driftPerDayC. Body heat is per person on the floor (living or working there); waste heat per point of a running room's heat effect. Comfort bands are the comfort factor a home feels by its floor's temperature, the first band its temperature is below.",
